      "Name": "body",
      "Html": "\u003Cstyle class=\u0022code-analysis-syntax\u0022\u003E\n.docs-content pre{overflow-x:auto;margin:1rem 0 1.75rem;padding:1.25rem 1.4rem;border:1px solid rgba(20,42,72,.16);border-left:4px solid #0e6fae;border-radius:4px;background:#f7fbfe;color:#10263a}\n.docs-content pre code{white-space:pre;color:inherit;background:transparent;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.65}\n.language-csharp .syntax-comment{color:#587287;font-style:italic}.language-csharp .syntax-string{color:#8a3d12}.language-csharp .syntax-keyword{color:#6542a6;font-weight:700}.language-csharp .syntax-number{color:#096b65}.language-csharp .syntax-type{color:#0a6680;font-weight:600}\n\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIdentifier parameters must be named for their type, for example studentId.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhat the Standard says\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026ldquo;Naming Conventions\u0026rdquo; \u0026mdash; Identifiers are named for the model they identify. A name such as studentId preserves business meaning at the call site and avoids ambiguous parameters such as id. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://github.com/hassanhabib/The-Standard/blob/master/2.%20Services/2.%20Services.md#2034-naming-conventions\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003Eread it here\u003C/a\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhy it matters\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EA typed identifier still needs a domain-specific name because several identifiers often share the same primitive type. Naming it studentId prevents argument ambiguity and makes signatures readable without requiring a developer to inspect the implementation.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EBad code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Violates STX0017: Identifier parameters must be named for their type, for example studentId.\u003C/span\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Epublic\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E\u0026lt;\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGetStudent\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGuid\u003C/span\u003E id) =\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Edefault\u003C/span\u003E;\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EGood code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Follows STX0017\u003C/span\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Epublic\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E\u0026lt;\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGetStudent\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGuid\u003C/span\u003E studentId) =\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Edefault\u003C/span\u003E;\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E"
    }
